unknown argument `--wibble`. See `gleam run -m parrot -- --help`.

`--sqlite` needs a value. See `gleam run -m parrot -- --help`.

could not read `/app/gleam.toml`: Permission denied

`/app/gleam.toml` is not valid toml: expected a key but found =

`/app/gleam.toml` is not valid toml: `tools.parrot.output` is defined more than once

invalid gleam.toml: `name` is missing

invalid gleam.toml: `tools.parrot.output` has to be of type String, not Int

unknown engine: oracle. Expected postgresql, mysql or sqlite.

could not detect the database engine of the schema `priv/schema.sql`. Set `engine` in `[tools.parrot]` or pass `--engine`.

could not detect the database engine from the connection string in `DATABASE_URL`. It has to start with `postgres`, `mysql`, `sqlite:` or `file:`. Otherwise set `engine` in `[tools.parrot]` or pass `--engine`.

the environment variable `DATABASE_URL` is not set. Set it to the connection string of your database, or use `--sqlite <PATH>` or `--schema <PATH>`.

could not read `/app/src` while looking for queries: Permission denied

no queries were found in `/app/src`. Parrot looks for `*.sql` files inside of `sql` directories, f.e. `src/app/sql/users.sql`.

sqlite database `/app/app.db` does not exist

could not parse the connection string. Expected the format: mysql://user:password@host:port/database

could not fetch the database schema with `pg_dump`:
File not found: pg_dump

could not fetch the database schema with `pg_dump`:
exited with status 1, see its errors above

parrot can not download sqlc for freebsd amd64. If you have a sqlc binary, set `bin` in `[tools.parrot.sqlc]` or pass `--sqlc` with its path.

could not download sqlc from https://downloads.sqlc.dev/sqlc.tar.gz: could not connect, nxdomain

could not download sqlc from https://downloads.sqlc.dev/sqlc.tar.gz: the server responded with status 404

could not download sqlc from https://downloads.sqlc.dev/sqlc.tar.gz: the download does not contain a sqlc binary

the sqlc binary downloaded from https://downloads.sqlc.dev/sqlc.tar.gz does not match the expected checksum. This could mean the download was corrupted or tampered with.
expected: abc
received: def

could not save sqlc to `/app/build/.parrot/sqlc`: No space left on device

`sqlc` is not in the PATH. Install it, or remove `--sqlc system` and `bin = "system"` in `[tools.parrot.sqlc]` to let parrot download it.

could not run sqlc `/usr/bin/sqlc`: unknown command

could not call `sqlc generate`:
queries.sql:1:1: syntax error

could not call `sqlc generate`:
exited with status 1

could not access `/app/build/.parrot`, which parrot uses to run sqlc: Permission denied

could not read the output of sqlc: unexpected end of input
This is most likely a bug in parrot, please open an issue: https://github.com/daniellionel01/parrot/issues

could not write the generated module `/app/src/app/sql.gleam`: Permission denied

could not format the generated module `/app/src/app/sql.gleam`:
error: Syntax error
